                "text": "Analyse the examples:\nIn example 1:\nInput has non-zero rows at:\nrow 4: [0,0,8,0,0,0,0,0,8,0,0,0,0,0,8,0,0,0,0]\nrow 5: [8,8,8,...]\nrow 6: [0,0,0,0,0,8,0,0,0,0,0,8,0,0,0,0,0,8,0]\nNotice that rows 4, 5, 6 form a 3-row pattern.\nIn output:\nrow 0: matches row 6\nrow 1: matches row 4\nrow 2: matches row 5\nrow 3: matches row 6\nrow 4: matches row 4\nrow 5: matches row 5\nrow 6: matches row 6\nrow 7: matches row 4\n...\nWait! Look at the period:\nrow 4 is row 4, row 5 is row 5, row 6 is row 6.\nSo it's periodic with period 3!\nRow indices:\nr % 3 == 0: row 6 (since 6 % 3 = 0)\nr % 3 == 1: row 4 (since 4 % 3 = 1)\nr % 3 == 2: row 5 (since 5 % 3 = 2)\n\nLet's check example 2:\nNon-zero rows:\nrow 3: [2,0,2,0,...]\nrow 4: [2,2,2,2,...]\nrow 5: [2,0,2,0,...]\nHere rows 3, 4, 5 form a 3-row pattern.\nIn output:\nrow 0: matches row 3 (since 0 % 3 == 3 % 3 == 0)\nrow 1: matches row 4 (since 1 % 3 == 4 % 3 == 1)\nrow 2: matches row 5 (since 2 % 3 == 5 % 3 == 2)\nrow 3: matches row 3\nrow 4: matches row 4\nrow 5: matches row 5\n...\nSo it repeats vertically with period 3!\nWait, in example 1:\nrow 4 % 3 = 1 -> output row 1 is row 4.\nrow 5 % 3 = 2 -> output row 2 is row 5.\nrow 6 % 3 = 0 -> output row 0 is row 6.\nIt is literally extending the periodic 3-row pattern throughout the entire grid!\nSpecifically, the pattern in rows 4, 5, 6 (or 3, 4, 5) repeats every 3 rows (or whatever period the non-zero band is).\nWait, how tall is the pattern?\nIn example 1: rows 4, 5, 6 (height 3).\nIn example 2: rows 3, 4, 5 (height 3).\nAre all patterns height 3, or is it the height of the non-empty block?\nLet's see the test input when provided.Ready to evaluate test inputs. Please provide the test input grid.",
